        {
          "id": "the_twenty_six_pollutant_processes_are_three_roots_a_chain_and_three_sums",
          "description": "The run's whole scope, unpacked from `runspecpollutantprocess`, `runspecchainedto` and the three calculator constants rather than written down. THREE ROOTS: 101 (THC) and 601 (N2O) and 9101 (Total Energy Consumption) each carry a rate of their own, and 101's comes off `emissionratebyage` while the other two come off `emissionrate`. THREE CHAIN DEPTHS off 101: 501 (methane) and 7901 (NMHC) at depth 1, 8001 (NMOG) and 8701 (VOC) at 2, and the fourteen toxics at 3. TWO at depth 1 off 9101: 3101 (SO2), which MOVES declares in `runspecchainedto`, and 9001 (Atmospheric CO2), which it does not -- CO2AE carries its input pollutant as a Java constant and `run_chainDeclarationOverlap` asserts the two declarations never disagree. THREE SUMS -- 8601, 8801 and 9801 -- which have no multiplicative parent at all and are held out of the root resolution, because 8601 is the one pollutant-process in this run with TWO `runspecchainedto` rows and the parent join would otherwise sum 8001 and 501 into the nonsense id 8501. The twenty-seventh row, polProcessID 300001, is the mechanism pseudo-pollutant 3000: it is selected, it has no rate, no ratio and no summand, and it emits nothing.\n\nThis test pins six of the (pollutant, process) pairs -- the root, the three depth-3 toxics, NMHC and VOC -- and where each one's rate-row block starts. The chain inputs, roots and depths it used to assert at those rows are gone from the model (the chain is now the `lnk_*` edge list) and are not asserted here.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
