        {
          "id": "so2_is_the_fuel_sulfur_burned_scaled_by_the_energy_consumed",
          "description": "`SO2Calculator`, end to end. so2_calculator.rs:2079: SO2 = meanBaseRate x WsulfurLevel x energy / energyContent, where the first factor is `sulfateemissionrate` and the middle two are `SO2FuelCalculation1`'s market-share-weighted means over the county's fuel supply. Every number below except [5] is a cell of an INPUT table or of MOVESOutput; [5] is the port's own reading and is asserted as such.\n\nThe three sulfate rates are the whole of the model-year dependence: gasoline and ethanol carry 1.99378e-06 at every model year of this run, and diesel steps from 1.89735e-06 to 1.76298e-06 at 2007 -- which is a self-described `modelYearGroupID` band, 19502006 and 20072050, decoded rather than transcribed.\n\nELECTRICITY FAILS TWICE, and either one alone would produce the same 104-cohort block, so a fixture that checked one could not tell which MOVES used. Only the second is asserted here, at [5]; the first went with the assertions marked NOT CARRIED below. `sulfateemissionrate` has no fuelTypeID 9 row, so `rt_hasSulfateRate` is 0; and fuel subtype 90's `energyContent` is NULL, so `rt_supplyEnergyContent` is 0 and the division MariaDB would evaluate as NULL is guarded. Neither is inferred from the other.\n\nThe worked example: model year 2010 gasoline on the weekday. Total Energy is 10.7536 Million BTU, which is 10.7536 x 1,055,055.9 = 1.13466e+07 kJ, and 1.13466e+07 x 3.41892e-07 = 3.879 g of SO2 -- the reference's own figure to all six digits it stores.\n\nASSERTION BY ASSERTION.\n[1] rt_supplySulfurLevel: fuelformulation 9114's `sulfurLevel`, at market share 1.0. Reference table.\n[2] rt_supplySulfurLevel: The biodiesel blend 25003's 6.0 ppm. Reference table.\n[3] rt_supplyEnergyContent: fuelsubtype 12's `energyContent`. Reference table.\n[4] rt_supplyEnergyContent: fuelsubtype 21's. Reference table.\n[5] rt_supplyEnergyContent: Electricity. Subtype 90's `energyContent` is NULL, `SUM(marketShare * energyContent)` skips the NULL term, and `ff_energyContent` reads it as 0 -- so the market-share-weighted value is 0 although the formulation is supplied at share 1.0. The port's reading, not a reference cell (MOVES drops the table).\nNOT CARRIED: the sulfate-rate and SO2-factor assertions of the original list (`rt_sulfateBaseRate`, `rt_hasSulfateRate`, `rt_hasSo2Factor`, `rt_so2Factor`), because they name variables the model does not declare.\n[6] out_emissionQuant: Model year 2010 gasoline, weekday. MOVESOutput.\n[7] out_emissionQuant: Model year 2000 diesel, weekday -- the cell that reads the 19502006 band. MOVESOutput.\n[8] out_emissionQuant: The Total Energy Consumption the cell above is computed from, in Million BTU. It is asserted here because the SO2 factor is dimensionless in kilojoules and a reader has to see both ends of the conversion to check the example by hand.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplySulfurLevel",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 7.15,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1487
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplySulfurLevel",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1528
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyEnergyContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 41.696,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1487
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyEnergyContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 42.7,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1528
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyEnergyContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1610
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.out_emissionQuant",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 3.879,
              "coords": {
                "output_rows": 947
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.out_emissionQuant",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.00381515,
              "coords": {
                "output_rows": 997
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.out_emissionQuant",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 10.7536,
              "coords": {
                "output_rows": 2424
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "atmospheric_co2_and_co2_equivalent_are_two_ORDERED_steps_of_one_calculator",
          "description": "`CO2AERunningStartExtendedIdleCalculator`, both steps, and the ORDER between them is the point. Step 1a turns Total Energy into Atmospheric CO2; step 2 then reads `MOVESWorkerOutput` back -- INCLUDING the rows step 1a has just inserted -- and sums Atmospheric CO2, methane and N2O weighted by `globalWarmingPotential`. A port that ran step 2 off the energy would get the same three summands' weights and the wrong answer.\n\nTHE CARBON CHEMISTRY IS CHECKED AGAINST MOVES'S OWN INTERMEDIATE. The snapshot carries `carbonoxidationbyfueltype`, which is the calculator's `CarbonOxidationByFuelType` working table, and this document does not read it: `rt_supplyCarbonContent` and `rt_supplyOxidationFraction` are recomputed from `fuelsupply` and `fuelsubtype`, and the assertions below are that table's four rows -- 0.01982 / 1 on gasoline, 0.02022 / 1 on diesel, 0.0194 / 1 on ethanol and 0 / 0 on electricity.\n\nELECTRICITY IS EMITTED AT EXACTLY ZERO, which is the opposite of SO2's behaviour on the same cohort and is the one place the two stages can be told apart: `carbonContent` and `oxidationFraction` are REAL zeros rather than absent rows, so the row exists (asserted through its emitted zero), and the Atmospheric CO2 block is 125 cohorts where SO2's is 104. All 42 of those rows are zero and so are their CO2 Equivalent twins, because electricity has no methane row either.\n\nThe worked example: model year 2010 gasoline on the weekday. 1.13466e+07 kJ x 0.01982 x 1 x 44/12 = 824,529 g of CO2; then 1 x 824,529 + 28 x 20.5384 + 265 x 1.43409 = 825,484 g of CO2 Equivalent, which is MOVESOutput's figure to all six digits it stores. The methane and N2O terms are 0.07 % and 0.05 % of the total, so the sum is checked against the reference and each summand separately -- a CO2 Equivalent that had dropped both would still be within 0.12 % of the right answer.\n\nASSERTION BY ASSERTION.\n[1] rt_supplyCarbonContent: `carbonoxidationbyfueltype.sumcarbonContent` for fuel type 1, recomputed. Reference intermediate.\n[2] rt_supplyCarbonContent: Fuel type 2's row of the same table.\n[3] rt_supplyCarbonContent: Fuel type 5's.\n[4] rt_supplyCarbonContent: Fuel type 9's -- a REAL zero, not a missing row.\n[5] rt_supplyOxidationFraction: Fuel type 1's oxidation fraction, 1.\n[6] rt_supplyOxidationFraction: Fuel type 9's, a REAL zero.\n[7] out_emissionQuant: Atmospheric CO2, model year 2010 gasoline, weekday. MOVESOutput. (The factor 0.01982 x 1 x 44/12, on the EXACT ratio, is the port's own arithmetic and is no longer a variable; the MariaDB decimal 3.6667 would give 0.07268, and docs/chain-so2-co2e-mechanism.md 7.1 measures the difference.)\n[8] out_emissionQuant: Atmospheric CO2, model year 2010 electricity: emitted, and zero.\n[9] out_emissionQuant: CO2 Equivalent for the same gasoline cell. MOVESOutput. (The globalWarmingPotential weights, 1 / 28 / 265 and 0 for CO2 Equivalent's own NULL, are no longer variables and are checked only here.)\n[10] out_emissionQuant: CO2 Equivalent, electricity.\n[11] out_emissionQuant: The methane summand of that CO2 Equivalent. MOVESOutput.\n[12] out_emissionQuant: The N2O summand. MOVESOutput.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyCarbonContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.01982,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 3619
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyCarbonContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.02022,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 3660
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyCarbonContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0194,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 3701
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyCarbonContent",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 3742
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyOxidationFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 3619
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_supplyOxidationFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 3742
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.out_emissionQuant",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 824529.0,
              "coords": {
                "output_rows": 2299
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.out_emissionQuant",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "output_rows": 2403
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.out_emissionQuant",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 825484.0,
